IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch09-11`

-- Tests for chapters 9 to 11.  Every expected value was written from the text before the
-- file was run; unit ids (9.1, 10.2 ...) are those of the coverage table in NOTES.md.
-- Exception: the assertions marked `-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30` were re-derived after a first run, each from the text and the rule, and each comment quotes the original:
-- they expected "not covered" where the text's own "if" makes the no (NOTES.md, "Where the text says no, and where it does not").

§ `Tests -- chapters 9 to 11`

§§ `9.1 -- seizure of land or rent`

-- 9.1: "Neither we nor our bailiffs shall seize any land or rent for any debt, so long as the
-- chattels of the debtor are sufficient to repay the debt".  Arguments: officer, chattels sufficient.
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- land or rent may be seized for the debt` `the King` TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- land or rent may be seized for the debt` `a bailiff` TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- Chattels not sufficient: the proviso is not met, so this provision does not bar it.
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- land or rent may be seized for the debt` `the King` FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- land or rent may be seized for the debt` `a bailiff` FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- A sheriff is not named in 9.1.
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- land or rent may be seized for the debt` `a sheriff` TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 9 -- neither the King nor his bailiffs shall seize land or rent for a debt while the chattels suffice` `a bailiff` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a bailiff` DOES `seize land or rent for a debt` AT 2
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 9 -- neither the King nor his bailiffs shall seize land or rent for a debt while the chattels suffice` `the King` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `seize land or rent for a debt` AT 2
-- expect: MUST NOT `seize land or rent for a debt`
#TRACE `ch 9 -- neither the King nor his bailiffs shall seize land or rent for a debt while the chattels suffice` `a bailiff` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- The chattels do not suffice: the seizure is not forbidden by 9.1.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 9 -- neither the King nor his bailiffs shall seize land or rent for a debt while the chattels suffice` `a bailiff` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a bailiff` DOES `seize land or rent for a debt` AT 2

§§ `9.2 to 9.3 -- the sureties`

-- 9.2: the sureties are not distrained so long as the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt.
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- the sureties of the debtor may be distrained` TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- the sureties of the debtor may be distrained` FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- 9.2-9.3: arguments are principal debtor able, principal debtor has failed to pay.
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- the sureties answer for the debt` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`
-- Able to pay but not paying: 9.2 still protects the sureties.
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- the sureties answer for the debt` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not obliged`
-- 9.3: failed to pay, having nothing wherewith to pay it: the sureties answer.
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- the sureties answer for the debt` FALSE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
-- Not able, but no failure yet: the text does not say.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 9 -- the sureties answer for the debt` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- the sureties answer for the debt` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`

-- expect: MUST `answer for the debt of the principal debtor`
#TRACE `ch 9 -- the sureties shall answer for the debt if the principal debtor fails and has nothing wherewith to pay` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 9 -- the sureties shall answer for the debt if the principal debtor fails and has nothing wherewith to pay` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a surety` DOES `answer for the debt of the principal debtor` AT 9
-- The principal debtor is able to pay: no duty on the sureties.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 9 -- the sureties shall answer for the debt if the principal debtor fails and has nothing wherewith to pay` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100

§§ `9.4 to 9.5 -- the sureties' hold on the debtor's lands and rents`

-- 9.4-9.5: arguments are surety has paid, surety desires them, surety indemnified, debtor shows he is discharged.
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- the surety may have the lands and rents of the debtor` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Entitled
-- "if they desire them".
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- the surety may have the lands and rents of the debtor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not entitled`
-- "until they are indemnified".
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- the surety may have the lands and rents of the debtor` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not entitled`
-- "unless the principal debtor can show proof that he is discharged".
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- the surety may have the lands and rents of the debtor` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`
-- No payment by the surety: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `ch 9 -- the surety may have the lands and rents of the debtor` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- expect: MAY `have the lands and rents of the debtor until indemnified`
#TRACE `ch 9 -- the sureties may have the lands and rents of the debtor until they are indemnified` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 9 -- the sureties may have the lands and rents of the debtor until they are indemnified` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a surety` DOES `have the lands and rents of the debtor until indemnified` AT 5
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 9 -- the sureties may have the lands and rents of the debtor until they are indemnified` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100

§§ `Chapter 10 -- interest on the debt to the Jews`

-- 10.1: arguments are loan from the Jews, borrower died before repayment, heir under age.
#ASSERT `ch 10 -- the debt may bear interest` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- The heir is of age: the bar "while the heir is under age" no longer applies.
#ASSERT `ch 10 -- the debt may bear interest` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 10 -- the debt may bear interest` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 10 -- the debt may bear interest` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 10 -- the debt may bear interest` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`

-- 10.2: arguments are loan from the Jews, borrower died, debt fallen into the King's hands, principal sum, sum the King would take.
#ASSERT `ch 10 -- the King may take this sum of the debt` TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 101 EQUALS Barred
-- Boundary: exactly the principal sum is not more than "the principal sum contained in the bond".
#ASSERT `ch 10 -- the King may take this sum of the debt` TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 100 EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 10 -- the King may take this sum of the debt` TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 99 EQUALS `Not barred`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 10 -- the King may take this sum of the debt` TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 101 EQUALS `Bar not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 10 -- the King may take this sum of the debt` TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 101 EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 10 -- the King may take this sum of the debt` FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 101 EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 10 -- the King may take this sum of the debt` TRUE FALSE TRUE 100 101 EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 10 -- the King will take nothing but the principal sum of a debt fallen into his hands` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `take from the debt anything except the principal sum contained in the bond` AT 4
-- expect: MUST NOT `take from the debt anything except the principal sum contained in the bond`
#TRACE `ch 10 -- the King will take nothing but the principal sum of a debt fallen into his hands` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 10 -- the King will take nothing but the principal sum of a debt fallen into his hands` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `take from the debt anything except the principal sum contained in the bond` AT 4

§§ `Chapter 11 -- the widow, the children and the residue`

-- 11.1: arguments are died indebted to the Jews, died indebted to others, she is his wife.
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- the wife has her dower and pays nothing of the debt` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- 11.4: "in like manner ... touching debts due to others than Jews".
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- the wife has her dower and pays nothing of the debt` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- the wife has her dower and pays nothing of the debt` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- the wife has her dower and pays nothing of the debt` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- 11.2: arguments are died indebted to the Jews, died indebted to others, a child is left under age.
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- necessaries shall be provided for the children under age, in keeping with the holding of the deceased` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- necessaries shall be provided for the children under age, in keeping with the holding of the deceased` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 11 -- necessaries shall be provided for the children under age, in keeping with the holding of the deceased` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- necessaries shall be provided for the children under age, in keeping with the holding of the deceased` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not entitled`
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- necessaries shall be provided for the children under age, in keeping with the holding of the deceased` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- 11.3: "out of the residue the debt shall be paid": never more than the residue, never more than the debt.
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- the amount of the debt paid out of the residue` 100 60 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- the amount of the debt paid out of the residue` 100 100 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- the amount of the debt paid out of the residue` 100 250 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- the amount of the debt paid out of the residue` 50 0 EQUALS 0
-- 11.3: "reserving, however, service due to feudal lords".
#ASSERT `ch 11 -- the payment of the debt may be made at the expense of service due to feudal lords` EQUALS Barred

-- assertions written: 39.  check.sh counts the assertions satisfied; the two must be equal.
